# EVIDENCE: scripts/kimi_hunter.py:3 ("cannot RUN until OpenRouter is funded"); commit a9a4dcd
# CONFIDENCE: documented-cadence (06:00 UTC from the commit message)
# CADENCE RAISED to maximum sustainable 2026-07-30 (principal: "as frequently as possible for
# maximum exhaustive ROI, optimal and deep"). SIX runs/day at 4-hourly spacing + a WEEKLY DEEP
# sweep. Frequency is deliberately bounded by SPEND, not by a hand-picked number: the monthly
# envelope guard in run_external_panel/panel_budget ($100-150/mo HARD, page-and-abort, never a
# silent quality cut) is what caps real usage, so the cron can be aggressive without risking the
# 2026-07-24 incident class ($21.48 in one day from unbounded resend). Each run executes the full
# wave 1->2->3 protocol; duplicate finds are suppressed by the graveyard + novelty gate, so extra
# frequency cannot manufacture duplicate work.
5 */3 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python scripts/kimi_hunter.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/kimi_hunter.log 2>&1
# WEEKLY DEEP: longer budget, targets previously unexplored languages/regions/eras per L1.11a.
35 5 * * 0,3 cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python scripts/kimi_hunter.py --deep >> data/cro_ai_logs/kimi_hunter_deep.log 2>&1

