# ORDER-BOOK MICROSTRUCTURE STATE SCREEN (max_audit defect `unwired-caller`, 2026-08-05). Stage A
# only, zero promotion authority. The script carried its own intended cron line as a COMMENT --
# "ops/crontab.manifest is owned by another agent this wave, so this comment is the request, not
# the installation" (scripts/screen_orderbook_state.py:2-11) -- and the request was never picked
# up, so libs/research/orderbook_state.py had exactly one importer and that importer had no
# caller. The module was unreachable while the orphan check read green, which is the one-link-
# short failure the defect names. run_mechanism_census ranks this class #1 of 20 (gap 0.396,
# coverage NAMED-UNTESTED) against ~10 GB of L2 depth tape already on disk: the highest-value
# distinct mechanism the desk has never run, untested for want of a SCREEN, not for want of data.
# CADENCE CEILING: DATA-ARRIVAL. The pre-registered family is fixed and the tape only grows in
# calendar time, so a faster cadence re-reads unchanged partitions. Six-hourly at :23 keeps it
# off the recorders' rotation and off screen_moat.py.
# WHY choom AND nice, MEASURED 2026-08-05 ON THIS BOX -- this is not belt-and-braces, it is the
# only thing that makes the line safe to install here. Peak RSS is ~510-650 MB and essentially
# FLAT in --files (580 MB at 24, 652 MB at 240): the cost is the load path, not the budget. This
# box has 3.8 GB total with ~3.2 GB resident in desk processes, so ~500 MB free, and the screen
# was SIGKILLed by the kernel OOM killer at --files 48/96/160/240 in four consecutive probes. Six
# cashcarry_executor processes run here (oom_score 687-710, oom_score_adj 0), so an unguarded
# 650 MB job is a MONEY-PATH hazard: the kernel picks by score and the executor is a candidate.
# `choom -n 1000` makes the screen self-nominate as the preferred victim, so the worst case is
# that the screen dies and the book is untouched -- never the other way round. It exits 0 with a
# NOT-READABLE-HERE artifact on a box without data/moat, so the line is harmless anywhere.
# HONEST LIMITATION, ROWED not hidden: with ~500 MB free this box will usually kill the run
# before it finishes, so on THIS host the line is correct-but-starved rather than productive.
# The real fix is a bounded-memory load path (stream partitions instead of accumulating), which
# is beyond a wiring change -- see the ledger row raised with this commit. Wiring it guarded is
# still strictly better than leaving the module unreachable, and it runs to completion wherever
# the desk has ordinary headroom.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/screen_orderbook_state.py -> data/orderbook_state_screen.json (verified
#   status=SCREENED on a 24-file run 2026-08-05); libs/research/orderbook_state.py
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (cadence and budget as pre-registered by the script's own header)
# RETIRED 2026-09-05 under the MT5 universe mandate (2026-08-18):
# scripts/screen_orderbook_state.py was an axis screen over the retired crypto-exchange universe.
