# DENOMINATOR FENCE (L1.57). fence_exit fixed the map from STATUS to exit code; it cannot see a
# status that is honestly OK because the fence examined NOTHING -- an empty rglob yields zero
# violations NECESSARILY, and "I checked 900 files and found nothing" and "I checked nothing"
# printed the same line and returned the same code. Measured at build time: 18 of 40 fences pass
# vacuously, 10 more publish len(<hardcoded literal>) as a denominator. The proving instance was
# live: check_exploration reported OK with n_organs 0 because `len(fresh) < n / 2` is `0 < 0.0`.
# Verdicts: DECLARED / VACUOUS (a pass over an empty scan set -- the failing state) / UNDECLARED
# (counted against a coverage ratchet, not a failure). Zero declarations reads UNMEASURED, never
# OK; the fence is subject to its own law via scanned=n_fences. CADENCE: hourly, phased off
# check_input_provenance -- it reads a registry that only changes when another fence exits, so it
# is data-arrival bound on those runs (L1.28c) and is pure-CPU over one small JSONL.
