# TRADE REVIEW (R0139): the discretionary desk's LEARNING LOOP, on BINANCE perps. Reads each closed
# paper trade against what was claimed at entry -- thesis, named structure, falsifier, chart state
# -- and against what price then did, then classifies the cause into something actionable
# (THESIS-WRONG / LEVEL-WRONG / TIMING-WRONG / NOISE-STOP / RIGHT-AND-PAID / RIGHT-BUT-TRUNCATED /
# UNLUCKY) and extracts ONE falsifiable lesson. Weights are fixed and nothing here fine-tunes:
# what improves is the desk's evidence-weighted knowledge of WHICH SETUPS PAY, the way a journal
# improves a human. The playbook is an EVIDENCE LADDER -- PROVISIONAL on one observation with no
# authority, SUPPORTED only after 3 agreeing trades, RETIRED the moment one contradicts it (and the
# contradiction recorded so it cannot return), STALE if untested for 25 closed trades. ONLY
# SUPPORTED lessons reach the trading brief: one lucky trade must not rewrite the method.
# 3x/day, offset from the resolver so it reads freshly-closed trades.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/run_trade_review.py -> data/trading_playbook.json + data/trade_review.json
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle)
# RETIRED 2026-09-05 under the MT5 universe mandate (2026-08-18): scripts/run_trade_review.py was
# an ops/execution organ bound to the retired crypto executor and its Gate-0 staging ladder. The
# MT5 gateway carries its own cost, quality and guard path under desks/mt5/.
