# SURVIVOR BOTTLENECK PANEL -- every seat argues about why nothing has ever survived.
# The desk's root-cause finding (52 of 350 recorded negatives, 14.9%, were powered enough to mean
# anything) was produced by ONE reasoner, and a finding from one reasoner is exactly the thing most
# worth attacking. This puts the same measured artifacts in front of the GPT/CRO brain and every
# reachable OpenRouter family and makes them argue: round one alone, round two refuting each other
# ANONYMISED, then ranked by agreement that survived forced contradiction. Agreement between
# parallel monologues is a shared prior; agreement after refutation is evidence.
# GPT IS AN ADDITION, NEVER THE BRAIN: nothing here is executed, every response is DATA parsed into
# structured proposals, and the output is a ranked list for a person.
# EVERY PROPOSAL IS FENCED. A model asked "how do we get survivors" has one overwhelmingly easy
# answer -- lower the bar -- and it will find it. Anything loosening a gate, raising size, touching
# the deadman switch, selecting post hoc, or removing a validation stage is REFUSED and recorded
# with its reason (the refusal is kept, because a seat proposing it is information about the seat).
# CEILING TYPE (L1.28c) is INFORMATION-ARRIVAL: the dossier only moves when the screens, the
# type-II report or the forward clocks move, which is daily at most. Weekly, because a panel re-run
# against an unchanged dossier returns the same argument at full token cost. Sunday 06:40 sits
# after the week's screens and before the Monday research cycle reads them.
# SPEND: checked BEFORE any call against the monthly cap; a missing key writes a BLOCKED artifact
