# WEEKLY WHOLE-DESK GRADE -- 100% coverage PROVEN, scored harshly, every aspect pushed at once.
# The daily capability ratchet grades 26 aspects and names ONE binding constraint, which is right
# for a daily cadence. It has two limits a weekly grade must not inherit:
#   1. ITS ASPECT LIST IS ASSERTED, NOT PROVEN -- a hardcoded tuple of 26. An aspect nobody wrote
#      into it is invisible: scores nothing, drags no number down. This organ DERIVES the surface
#      (every cron organ, every libs package, every data artifact, every L1.x law) and reports what
#      NO aspect claims. FIRST LIVE RUN: 59 of 327 rated, 268 UNRATED -- including ALL NINE laws,
#      150 of 158 organs and 29 of 30 subsystems. The 26 numbers were grading 18% of the desk.
#   2. ITS HEADLINE IS AN ARITHMETIC MEAN -- 5.82 while alerting_pager sits at 0.0. An average lets
#      two 10s pay for a zero; capability is a CHAIN. Headline is the HARMONIC mean (0.98 on the
#      same numbers) MULTIPLIED by coverage, because a score computed over 18% of the surface is
#      worth 18% of its face value. First live grade: 0.17/10.
# Coverage is a MULTIPLIER, not another term -- as a term it diluted to 4.09 on a desk with nine of
# ten surfaces unrated, which would say a desk nobody has measured is middling.
# OUTPUT IS THE FULL WORKLIST, not the minimum: every aspect below 10 with its distance-to-ceiling
# and its own next action, with UNRATED surfaces ranked ABOVE every low score -- a part of the desk
