# --- L1.46 CLOCK PROVENANCE (capability hunt s0, 2026-08-01) --------------------------------
# CEILING TYPE (L1.28c): DATA-ARRIVAL bound, and the arrival granularity is EXACTLY ONE HOUR --
# the moat tape rotates hourly (data/moat/<venue>/<SYMBOL>/YYYYMMDD_HH.jsonl.gz), so the fence's
# unit of observation is one file per stream. Denser re-reads a file it has already judged;
# sparser lets a whole file be written wrong unseen, and an hour recorded without the venue stamp
# is a Delta hour that cannot be bought back at any price (L1.28b(f): the collector never
# throttles, so the detector must not either). Hourly is therefore the ceiling AND the floor.
# PHASE :40 -- mid-file, deliberately. At :05 the newest file holds ~5 minutes and the achieved-
# period estimate is thin; at :40 it holds ~40 minutes, which is a solid median over ~300 depth
# rows, while still catching a bad hour inside that hour rather than after it.
# Pure CPU: samples 4 symbols per venue and reads the FRONT of each gzip, so it stops early
# instead of decompressing 7.5GB -- the cost of running it is a rounding error.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/check_clock_provenance.py -> data/clock_provenance_status.json; CONSTITUTION L1.46
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle; first run fired MIXED-CLOCK and named fut/* and
# spot/* as interleaving two clocks under one field name, and independently reproduced the
# achieved-vs-configured period gap on both Binance recorders -- 8.28s and 7.84s against 5.0s)
40 * * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_clockprov.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/check_clock_provenance.py --report-only >> data/cro_ai_logs/clock_provenance.log 2>&1

# KERNEL-LOG READABILITY FENCE (R0350) -- the same L1.40 "unmeasured must never read as OK"
# doctrine as check_clock_provenance above, applied to the input every kill/OOM diagnosis starts
# from. Readability drifts under this environment: dmesg was denied outright on 2026-08-01, and on
# the current box dmesg reads while `journalctl -k` returns no journal files at all. When no
# channel is readable, "no OOM found" is not a finding -- it is a measurement that did not happen,
# and this fence says so instead of letting silence read as health.
# Daily, not hourly: readability changes on reboots and image swaps, not within a day, and the
# probe shells out to dmesg.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/check_kernel_log.py -> data/kernel_log_status.json; ledger R0350 (unblocked
# 2026-08-04 when the box became root-capable, which is itself the drift the fence guards).
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (first run on this box: dmesg readable with 354 lines, journalctl-k
# rc 0 but ZERO lines -> correctly recorded unreadable, since an empty successful read proves
# nothing; verdict READABLE on the surviving channel)
25 5 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python scripts/check_kernel_log.py --json --report-only >> data/cro_ai_logs/kernel_log.log 2>&1

