# CROSS-SECTIONAL FUNDING SNAPSHOT (R0119 producer -- the crowding denominator).
# `current_funding()` returns all ~855 USD-M perps at ONE instant and five production callers
# fetch it, rank it, trade off it and DISCARD it. Without the universe at the same instant there
# is no residual to take, so "are our own names being crowded?" is structurally unanswerable.
# CADENCE CEILING: DATA-ARRIVAL. `premiumIndex` is a SNAPSHOT endpoint serving no history, so an
# uncollected hour is permanently unbuyable (L1.28b(f)) -- but the underlying rate only moves
# meaningfully across settlement stamps, the fastest of which on this venue is 4h. Hourly
# over-samples that deliberately: it costs one keyless REST call, it clears the fence's 8-snapshot
# floor within 8h of a position opening, and a FIXED minute keeps every snapshot at a consistent
# funding phase so a drift measure is not reading its own sampling phase.
# PHASE :07 -- not aligned to any funding stamp (00/04/08/12/16/20 UTC), and clear of the :4x
# fence cluster so the tape is already written when check_crowding reads it at :46.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/collect_funding_cross_section.py -> data/funding_cross_section.jsonl; §42
# RETIRED 2026-09-05 under the MT5 universe mandate (2026-08-18):
