# POINT-IN-TIME UNIVERSE SNAPSHOT (R0239). list_perp_symbols filters exchangeInfo to
# status == TRADING and discards the rest, so every backfilled panel is conditioned on the symbol
# SURVIVING to the day the backfill ran -- textbook survivorship bias. First capture (2026-08-01)
# found 851 symbols of which 124 were NOT trading (123 SETTLING, 1 PENDING): 14.6% of the universe
# was invisible to every cross-sectional study the desk has ever run.
# WHY DAILY AND WHY IT CANNOT SLIP: a point-in-time snapshot not taken today cannot be taken
# tomorrow. Unlike almost every other job here, a missed run is not stale data -- it is a
# permanent hole. The value is continuity, so the series only becomes worth something by being
# unbroken. The exchangeInfo call already happens on every ingest and was being thrown away.
# SCOPE, honestly: this fixes the panel FORWARD. It does NOT restore LUNA/UST/FTT/SRM to the
# seven-year history -- that reconstruction from binance.vision delisted archives is a separate,
# larger job and should be scoped once rather than implied here.
# 00:20 UTC: early enough that the snapshot describes the day it is named for, clear of midnight.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/snapshot_universe.py -> data/universe_snapshots.jsonl.gz (append-only)
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (first run recorded 851 symbols across 3 statuses)
# RETIRED 2026-09-05 under the MT5 universe mandate (2026-08-18): scripts/snapshot_universe.py
# was a crypto-exchange/on-chain data collector. The venue it read is retired ground and the
