# R0104 CAPABILITY RATCHET (owed-work, 2026-08-05). The principal's standing order -- every aspect
# of the desk pushed toward 10/10 every day, non-exhaustively -- had NO INSTRUMENT: the per-aspect
# rating existed only in conversation, so it could not ratchet, a fall left no trace, and nothing
# ever named what was holding an aspect down. This scores nine named aspects from artifacts other
# organs already write, keeps a high-water mark per aspect AND per component, and prints the
# quantified next thing that buys one more point. A FALL exits 2 with a NAMED CAUSE (which
# component, from what to what, out of which file); a FLATLINE is reported with its binding
# constraint; UNMEASURED is its own state and is never scored as 0 and never as 10.
# 09:50 UTC: downstream of everything it reads -- the 06:xx-07:xx governance block, the 08:xx
# collectors and the 09:30 capability hunt are all in by then -- and clear of the 10:00 data-axis
# dig and the 10:10 commit audit. Deliberately NOT --report-only: a regression must leave a
# non-zero exit in the log, which is the whole difference between a ratchet and a report.
# CEILING TYPE (L1.28c) is INFORMATION-ARRIVAL and daily is AT it: every input (audit report, law
# gate, gate0 readiness, mutation score, ledger, liveness) moves at most once a day, so a second
# run would re-read the same numbers and record the same marks.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/run_capability_ratchet.py -> data/CAPABILITY_RATCHET.json; first live reading
# 2026-08-05 scored 9/9 aspects (mean 5.7/10, alpha_output 0.8 the lowest, risk_rails 9.3 the
# highest) and named 2 UNMEASURED components -- the budget-truncated autodiscovery mutation target
# and the BLOCKED-UNKNOWN ruin rail. CONFIDENCE: measured (that reading is from the run itself).
