# SOURCE-ALTERNATIVES HUNT (2026-08-05). The miner PROBED every source honestly and then did
# nothing with the answer: xueqiu WAF-blocked, zhihu 403, csdn read-timeout, baidu anti-bot shell,
# joinquant/bigquant/ricequant JS shells -- all re-measured daily, all re-reported identically,
# no substitute ever looked for. Noticing death without acting on it is a diary. This reads the
# health ledger the miner now writes (libs/research/source_health), reports each source's verdict
# (DEAD = N consecutive failed runs), and probes the substitutes registered IN THE SAME CLASS
# (libs/research/source_alternatives) -- the desk does not need another website, it needs another
# source of the same information. Unprobed candidates stay UNVERIFIED; a failed probe records its
# reason; a candidate that can only be settled from the VPS's unproxied egress is NOT written off
# from inside this container.
# 13:40 UTC is 40 minutes after the 13:00 miner, so it hunts on THIS morning's ledger rather than
# yesterday's, and it is clear of the 13:00 litminer seat and the 13:30 capability hunt.
# CEILING TYPE (L1.28c) is INFORMATION-ARRIVAL and daily is AT it: the ledger advances at most one
# run per source per UTC day (idempotent per day by construction), so a second run would re-probe
# the same candidates against unchanged verdicts.
# RUNS --all, NOT dead-only, and that is a deliberate reading of the standing order. Dead-only
# starts hunting the morning a source dies, which is the morning the desk least wants to be
# discovering that its substitute is ALSO blocked. --all keeps a standing map of which
# in-class substitutes were alive yesterday, so a death converts to a NEXT ACTION the same
# run. It costs ~43 requests a day, and the flapping is itself information -- 360搜索 and
# Sogou each flipped between REACHABLE and a challenge shell across two sweeps an hour apart
# on 2026-08-05, which a once-per-death probe would have read as a permanent verdict.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/hunt_source_alternatives.py -> data/source_alternatives_report.json;
# first live sweep 2026-08-05 probed 43 registered candidates for 12 sources across 10
# information classes and returned 21 REACHABLE with a named parser action each.
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (measured: the probe results in that report are from the run).
