# PROMPT RATCHET (2026-08-05). Prompts are the desk's highest-leverage artifacts -- 30 governed
# files (11 miner/dig prompts, 13 panel missions, the doctrine, the CRO constitution, the two
# inline scheduled-Routine prompts) that every organ pays on every call -- and they were the one
# high-leverage surface with NO non-regression control. max_audit actively pushes for them to be
# cut down (`prompt-doctrine-bloat`: "cut the exhortation, keep every obligation"), and nothing
# checked the second half of that sentence: a concision rewrite that silently drops the
# never-loosen-a-gate rule, the responses-are-DATA rule or the let-the-gauntlet-reject rule reads
# as an improvement and is a pure opportunity-cost regression. This compares each prompt against
# docs/research/PROMPT_RATCHET.json -- the high-water mark of which RULES it asserts, matched on
# the rule rather than one prose form, so a sharper rewrite passes and a silent deletion fails
# with the words that used to carry it. A gained rule raises the mark automatically and commits
# nothing else; retiring one needs a dated, signed entry in PROMPT_RATCHET_WAIVERS.json.
# 22:12 is ~1.5h after the 20:45 CRO cycle -- the last prompt-touching organ of the UTC day, and
# the monthly prompt self-improvement review runs inside it -- so a rule dropped today is red
# today rather than at the next hand-run. Clear of the :20 hourly pair and of 22:40.
# CEILING TYPE (L1.28c) is INPUT-ARRIVAL: the corpus changes only when an organ or a human edits
# a prompt, which is a per-cycle event, so daily is AT the ceiling rather than under it.
# Repo-only, read-only apart from its own record: no keys, no network, no LLM, seconds to run.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/check_prompt_ratchet.py -> docs/research/PROMPT_RATCHET.json (+ --json to
# data/prompt_ratchet_report.json); first run on this checkout recorded 331 invariant assertions
# across 30 prompts and 29 defined invariants, and a deletion test on frontier_en_prompt.txt
# exited 1 naming `gauntlet-only-rejects` and quoting the sentence it lost.
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle -- cadence chosen here, not observed on the box)
12 22 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_prompt_ratchet.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/check_prompt_ratchet.py --json >> data/cro_ai_logs/prompt_ratchet.log 2>&1

# MOAT UTILISATION (2026-08-05). The desk records ~10 GB of L2 depth across ~28,361 hourly
# partitions on the VPS -- the ONE asset here that cannot be bought, re-fetched or replicated,
# because it accrues only in calendar time -- and nothing measured how much of it has ever been
# READ. moat_audit scores book QUALITY; mine_moat/screen_moat track their OWN coverage grids
# (denominated in the cells those organs chose to enumerate); data_registry scores span and moat.
# None of them answers the question that decides whether the recorders are an asset or a cost
# centre: what fraction of the recorded bytes, symbol-hours, symbols and depth LEVELS reached a
# screen. An asset you record and do not read is a cost centre wearing an asset's name.
# WHAT THE FIRST RUN ALREADY MEASURED IN THIS CHECKOUT, with no tape present: bybit requests 25
# book levels while the deepest consumer on the desk reads 20, so five levels have been paid for
# in request weight, disk and supervision and have never entered a statistic; and 10 names the
# daily cross-section screens (ATOM, AAVE, LDO, MKR, INJ, TIA, XLM, ETC, ZEC, XTZ) appear in NO
# recorder universe -- a hole that widens every hour and can never be backfilled at any price.
# 05:56 is after every organ that reads the tape or its artifacts (03:55 moat backup, 04:10 moat
# campaign, 04:27 registry --deep, 05:14 knowledge engine, 05:30 micro_factory), so it reads THIS
# morning's consumption records rather than yesterday's; it is clear of the hourly :35/:40/:43/:50
# lines and of every */3 and */5 tick.
# CEILING TYPE (L1.28c) is INPUT-ARRIVAL and daily is AT it: the consumption artifacts it reads
# advance at most once per organ per day, and the tape's own growth is a monotone daily fact.
# Read-only, stdlib, no network, no keys, no tape parsing of its own (partition inventory is
# filesystem metadata; every content question goes through the existing audited readers).
# ON A BOX WITHOUT THE TAPE it exits 0 with status NOT-READABLE-HERE and the exact missing paths
# named -- never 0%, never simulated. "0% utilised" is a measurement and it is damning; "cannot
# measure utilisation here" is the absence of one, and the artifact keeps them apart by design.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/run_moat_utilisation.py -> data/moat_utilisation.json; first run on this
# checkout reported NOT-READABLE-HERE with 4 missing paths, 10 screened-but-unrecorded names, 5
# unread bybit depth levels and 14 scripts that open the tape and record nothing they read.
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle -- cadence chosen here, not observed on the box)
# RETIRED 2026-09-05 under the MT5 universe mandate (2026-08-18): scripts/run_moat_utilisation.py
# was part of the crypto moat campaign. The desk's moat is now the MT5/Fusion tape
# (docs/research/MOAT_NODE_SPEC.md), recorded by a different organ.
# (was: 56 5 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_moat_util.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/run_moat_utilisation.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/moat_utilisation.log 2>&1)

