# THREE STAGE-A SCREENS THAT WERE BUILT AND THEN NOT RUN (2026-08-05).
#
# Each of these shipped with an "INTENDED CADENCE (NOT wired here -- the manifest is owned by
# another pass)" comment in its own header. Every one of those comments was correct about the
# ownership and wrong about the outcome: the request was written, the wave ended, and nobody
# converted it. check_unwired_modules found all three at once -- each the SOLE importer of a
# library module, so the module was unreachable and the orphan check stayed green anyway.
#
# That is the conversion defect in its purest form. The research was done, the pre-registration
# was sealed, the code passed its gates, and the desk received EXACTLY NOTHING, because the last
# link was left as a note. A screen that is never scheduled is indistinguishable from a screen
# that was never written, except that it cost more. The cadences below are the ones each script
# asked for, in its own header, verbatim -- there is no new judgement here, only the conversion.
#
# CEILING TYPE (L1.28c) is INPUT-ARRIVAL for all three and each is AT it: the diffusion screen
# advances only as announcements land (daily collector), and both weekly screens read inputs that
# move on a venue's or a project's announcement, not on a market clock.
