# FOUR MORE ORGANS THAT ASKED TO BE SCHEDULED AND WERE NOT (2026-08-05, second batch).
#
# Same pattern as the three Stage-A screens above, and finding it twice in one day is the point:
# every one of these shipped with "INTENDED CADENCE (NOT wired here -- the manifest is owned by
# another agent this wave, so this comment is the REQUEST, not the installation)". The comment is
# correct about ownership and, left alone, it is the whole failure -- the wave ends, the owner
# never converts the request, and finished work sits unreachable at a higher cost than never
# having been built. L1.53 names the general case; this is the acquisition side of it.
#
# The collector/screen PAIRS matter here. A screen wired without its collector reads an empty
# ledger forever and reports NOT-READABLE-HERE truthfully while buying nothing, which is the
# quietest way to look busy. Each pair is installed together and phased so the screen runs after
# the collector has landed the day it will read.
