# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRINCIPAL DROP -- the one intake route the desk's organs structurally cannot build for
# themselves. conversion_max reports mined_research total 14: FOURTEEN mined items have ever been
# READ, against a miner surfacing 60-115 rows six times a day. The chain mine -> rank -> [nobody
# reads] -> hypothesis -> screen -> survivor breaks at the read step, which is the whole answer to
# why the Chinese miner has produced no survivors while working perfectly.
#
# Reading is blocked differently per source and only one class is unbuildable: video is genuinely
# unreadable here (0 of 14 expose captions unauthenticated), Juejin bodies need browser rendering
# (a COST -- Chromium is present), and CLOSED GROUPS need a membership, which is a person and not
# a credential. This organ covers the third and says so.
#
# Hourly because the input is a human dropping a file: the cost is a directory listing on an empty
# inbox (microseconds, no network, no keys), and the alternative is material sitting unscored until
# tomorrow. CEILING TYPE (L1.28c) is INPUT-ARRIVAL and hourly is comfortably at it.
# PRIVACY: data/inbox and reports/principal_drop.json are BOTH gitignored, explicitly and
# separately from the blanket data/* rule, because publishing a closed group's contents to a
# remote cannot be undone by a later commit. A test asserts both entries survive.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/ingest_principal_drop.py -> reports/principal_drop.json
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle; verified on a synthetic WeChat export -- two
#   substantive messages scored 7.0/5.0, weather chatter correctly dropped)
19 * * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_drop.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/ingest_principal_drop.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/principal_drop.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# JOIN-LINK HARVEST -- the miner finds the doors, the principal walks through them.
#
# The miners index the OPEN web; the material that converts lives in CLOSED rooms no engineering
# reaches, because a membership is a person and not a credential. But those rooms ADVERTISE on the
# open web -- a t.me link in a DCInside thread, a discord.gg in a Qiita post -- and the miners were
# already fetching those pages and discarding the links. This closes the loop:
#   miner -> invite link -> ntfy push -> PRINCIPAL JOINS -> drops content -> ingest_principal_drop
# The desk cannot join anything and never will; it can say which door looks worth a person's time.
#
# RANKED BY CONTEXT, because most invite links on the open web advertise paid-signal groups --
# that is WHY they advertise. A link is scored by the surrounding text through the same
# video_triage ranker as everything else, and only links clearing the miner's own threshold push.
# ONE push per batch, never one per link, and de-duplicated permanently against
# data/join_links.jsonl: a pager that re-sends the same invite every cycle gets muted, and this
# desk has already lost 11.5 days of alerting to a pager nobody was reading.
# 07:31 -- after the 06:xx-07:xx mining and governance block, so it reads the morning's queue.
# CEILING TYPE (L1.28c) is INPUT-ARRIVAL and daily is at it: links appear only when a fetched page
# happens to carry one, and re-scanning an unchanged queue finds the same nothing.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/harvest_join_links.py -> reports/join_links.json
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle; detector verified on t.me/discord.gg/open.kakao
#   shapes, 0 false positives on bare-domain junk)
31 7 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_joinlinks.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/harvest_join_links.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/join_links.log 2>&1

