# AXIS-SCREEN CORRECTION LAYER -- the single unrun organ standing between this desk and its first
# forward clock, and it was never scheduled at all (0 cron lines before today).
#
# THE CHAIN IT BREAKS WHEN IT DOES NOT RUN, traced 2026-08-05:
#   finalize_axis_screens CRASHES on a missing screen file (unguarded read_text)
#     -> no report carries `verdict_adjusted`
#     -> run_paper_sleeve_spawner REFUSES ("NONE carries verdict_adjusted")
#     -> no Stage-A candidate can be admitted to a forward slot
#     -> 0 clocks ever started; 10 of 12 Stage-B slots idle; accruing = 0
#     -> NOTHING CAN EVER SURVIVE, because the two-stage law gives Stage B SOLE promotion
#        authority and Stage B had never been fed.
# Zero survivors was therefore structural, not statistical: no gate was too tight, the road to a
# survivor had simply never been opened.
#
# Runs after the Stage-A screens land (announcement diffusion 06:40, unlock series Mon 06:25,
# venue subsidy Mon 06:53) and BEFORE the spawner, so a corrected verdict is available the same
# morning it is produced rather than a day later.
# CEILING TYPE (L1.28c) is INPUT-ARRIVAL and daily is at it: corrections advance only when a
# screen re-runs, and re-correcting an unchanged artifact rewrites the same numbers.
# Pure CPU, stdlib, reads reports/axis_screens/*.json and rewrites them in place.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/finalize_axis_screens.py -> reports/axis_screens/*.json (verdict_adjusted)
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (first successful run 2026-08-05: corrected
#   liquidation_reversion_BTCUSDT, 6 trials, 0 surviving -- and the spawner then reported
#   NO-CANDIDATES, which is the honest state rather than a refusal)
