# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BYBIT L2 ARCHIVE RETENTION ALARM -- is the free 349-day backfill EXPIRING while we wait?
#
# quote-saver.bycsi.com is Bybit's first-party publication of its own L2 book at 200 levels /
# 100ms / 24h -- 8x the depth and 41x the resolution of our own recorder, which makes the desk's
# headline "irreplaceable Bybit L2" claim false: our copy is a strictly-worse subsample of a free
# file. The 2026-08-01 data-moat sweep measured the earliest available BTCUSDT date at 2025-08-21
# and INFERRED that retention might be ROLLING, in which case every day of delay destroys a day
# of free history permanently. That inference set R0243's entire urgency and nothing tested it.
#
# The row's own remedy was "run three HEAD probes on 2026-08-08" -- a diary entry. This is the
# probe as an organ: it bisects the earliest available date (~11 HEAD requests/symbol, no body
# transferred) and FAILS LOUD (exit 2) only when the boundary has ADVANCED since the last run.
# First real verdict 2026-08-05: FIXED. Boundary 2025-08-21 unmoved against the sweep's own
# 2026-08-01 measurement while the span GREW 345 -> 349 days from the recent end.
#
# CEILING TYPE (L1.28c) is DATA-ARRIVAL and daily is at it: the archive publishes T+1 (measured
# last-modified 00:03:45 UTC for the prior day), so the boundary can move at most once a day and
# firing more often re-reads an unchanged answer. 03:20 -- after publication, before the morning
# research block that would act on a ROLLING verdict.
# A network failure reports UNREACHABLE and exits 0 by design: a probe that cannot see is not
# evidence of a change, and a fence red on every blip gets switched off (L1.43).
# EVIDENCE: scripts/probe_bybit_archive.py -> data/bybit_archive_retention.json (committed, so a
#   wiped data/ cannot silently disarm the baseline the alarm is measured against)
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script + 10 tests, including the partial-outage case that would otherwise
#   converge on a too-recent boundary and shout ROLLING
# RETIRED 2026-09-05 under the MT5 universe mandate (2026-08-18). Bybit venue archive probe;
# Bybit may never be hunted again and the script was deleted with the desk.
# (was: 20 3 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && flock -n data/.cron_bybit_archive.lock .venv/bin/python scripts/probe_bybit_archive.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/bybit_archive.log 2>&1)

