# 517 -- 4455 dead names, two venues carrying MORE dead than live. Those are systematically the
# LOSERS, so every cross-section conditioned on today's listings is biased upward.
# CADENCE (L1.28c): INFORMATION-ARRIVAL. Delistings land in daily batches, so daily is the ceiling;
# faster re-reads an unchanged roster. The roster is a monotone UNION (never overwritten), so the
# only irreversible loss is a name that appears AND ages off between two runs -- daily bounds that
# to 24h. 03:35 -- after the bybit retention probe, same venue-truth block.
# A network failure records UNREACHABLE per venue, never ABSENT: "we could not ask" and "there is
# nothing there" demand opposite responses, and only an ENTIRELY unreachable run exits non-zero.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/probe_delisted_instruments.py -> data/delisted_instruments.json (registry)
#   + data/delisted_rosters/<venue>.json (the dead names themselves -- a count would be a
#   catalogue, and a catalogue is half a deliverable)
