# --- CROSS-SECTION FLOOR (L1.62 family) --------------------------------------------------------
# A per-date cross-sectional collapse over a thin cross-section is one symbol's noise, and
# consecutive thin dates give the resulting SERIES structure the data never had. The dominant
# guard in this repo is `if panel.shape[1] < N`, which counts DECLARED COLUMNS -- a 373-column
# panel clears it on a date carrying six finite names. It reads like a breadth guard and checks a
# number that cannot fall when the cross-section empties.
# CADENCE: daily. Its input is the repo's own source, which changes on every push, so it is
# INFORMATION-ARRIVAL bound (L1.28c). Phased to 06:57, after the 06:53 panel-breadth fence it
# extends. A pre-push hook would be the event-driven end state; daily is the honest start.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/check_cross_section_floor.py -> data/cross_section_floor.json; CONSTITUTION
# L1.62 family (matrix entry in build_enforcement_matrix.py).
