# --- RISK UNITS ON THE SIZING PATH (L1.67) -----------------------------------------------------
# A stop distance multiplied by the wrong instrument's contract size produces a lot that is
# well-formed, fresh, internally consistent and wrong by three orders of magnitude. Every MT5
# sizing function priced every sleeve as `dist * CONTRACT_OZ * FX_EUR` = 92.00 -- gold's contract
# times a frozen EUR/USD rate -- against a measured 0.86 (BTCUSD) to 86,414 (EURUSD) EUR per price
# unit per lot. Live, not latent: sleeve_set rewrites promoted sleeves to "auto_ramp", so the
# promoter's literal 0.01 never reaches the venue. Measured at EUR 1,683.89, a promoted CADJPY
# sleeve sized 0.46 lot, logged 1.26% risk and ran 7.41%, and cap_by_heat admitted three for a
# believed 2.94% book against a true 22.2%.
# CADENCE: daily. Its inputs are the universe snapshot (re-fetched at most daily) and gateway.py
# (changed by commits, not by the clock), so it is INFORMATION-ARRIVAL bound (L1.28c) -- firing
# hourly would re-read an unchanged AST. Phased to 06:59, after the 06:53 panel-breadth fence.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/check_risk_units.py -> data/risk_units.json; CONSTITUTION L1.67
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script (new this cycle); positive control PASSES against the pre-fix
# gateway (CONSTANT-ON-SIZING-PATH at auto_lot:203 and realised_q:187, plus 5 call sites
# defaulting to gold), and the first post-fix run reads OK over 22 priced symbols / 6 call sites.
59 6 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python scripts/check_risk_units.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/risk_units.log 2>&1

# --- ONE DRAWDOWN SOLVER, NOT FIVE (GAP 117) ---------------------------------------------------
# `if max_dd(q) > target: hi = q else: lo = q` reads RUIN as a passed check: past the point where
# some day has 1 + q*x <= 0 the account is gone, cumprod goes negative, the drawdown expression is
# NaN, and `NaN > target` is False -- so the search sizes UP. push_ceiling returned q = 2.0000 on
# every arm, CAGR +inf and -100%. mt5desk/sizing.py was made the single implementation on 08-19;
# two more copies survived into the merged tree from MASTER (exit_sweep, pyramid_sweep) and a
# third objective-variant sat in admission.py. Grep found the first two; only this fence found
# admission, and only after its own positive control caught the fence not working at all.
# CADENCE: daily. Its input is the source tree, which changes on commits rather than on the clock
# (L1.28c). Phased to 06:57, before the 06:59 risk-units fence.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/check_private_bisection.py -> data/private_bisection.json; GAP_REGISTER 117
# CONFIDENCE: committed-script + positive control -- tests/test_check_private_bisection.py carries
# the shipped bug verbatim and asserts it is flagged, plus rename/nancumprod/BOM variants. That
# control is load-bearing: the first version of this fence matched only outermost callees, missed
# `np.maximum.accumulate`, scanned 1,362 files and reported a clean tree that meant nothing.
57 6 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python scripts/check_private_bisection.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/private_bisection.log 2>&1

# --- VALIDATED AND ACCRUING NOTHING (GAP 119) --------------------------------------------------
# The ladder's rungs each report their own success and nobody owns the JOIN: a sweep prints
# "4 survivors" and exits 0, shadow prints its ledger and exits 0, and a cell that cleared a gate
# but was never added to shadow_forward.SLEEVES is invisible in both. III.16 applied to evidence.
# CADENCE: daily, after the hunts and before shadow's own run.
# EVIDENCE: desks/mt5/research/shadow_gap.py -> desks/mt5/shadow_gap.json
# CONFIDENCE: exit 2 when NO GATED CELL is readable -- reports/ is gitignored, and "0 missing"
# with an empty denominator is absence read as a clean verdict. It tests the denominator, not the
# file count; the first version tested the file count and printed a vacuous all-clear.
5 7 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT/desks/mt5" && "$QUANT_ROOT/.venv/bin/python" research/shadow_gap.py >> "$QUANT_ROOT/data/cro_ai_logs/shadow_gap.log" 2>&1

