53 6 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python scripts/check_bar_span.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/bar_span.log 2>&1

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COST-BASIS FENCE + COST SURFACE (added 2026-08-29, capability hunt s0)
# EVIDENCE: desks/mt5/research/cost_surface.py -> desks/mt5/data/cost_surface.json
#           scripts/check_cost_surface.py      -> data/cost_surface_report.json
# WHAT WAS MISSING: `universe.json:median_spread_pts` is ONE scalar per symbol for all 24 hours,
# collapsed at ingest, and it is the number every gate, certificate, stress scenario and forward
# clock divides by. Nothing anywhere compared a cell's CHARGED cost against the spread its own
# fill bars recorded. First run (2026-08-29) found both LIVE ZAR forward clocks undercharged --
# USDZAR 2.51x, EURZAR 2.10x on their own fill bars -- and both go NEGATIVE when re-priced at the
# desk's own declared honest baseline. 920 of 3,424 measured symbol-hour cells are material,
# 244 of them OVERCHARGED, which is the false-null direction that raises no alert anywhere else.
# CADENCE: surface first (it is a re-aggregation of the parquets the fetchers just wrote), fence
# immediately after it, both before the research day and before shadow_forward's pass at 07:58.
# CONFIDENCE: inferred slot; the ORDER is the load-bearing part, not the minute. The fence exits 2
# on COST-BASIS-MISMATCH, SURFACE-MISSING, STALE and UNMEASURED, and never renders an unmeasured
# cell as OK (L1.28a). NOT-READABLE-HERE is its own status so a box without the parquets cannot
# report a clean verdict about the desk.
20 6 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python desks/mt5/research/cost_surface.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/cost_surface.log 2>&1
35 6 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python scripts/check_cost_surface.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/cost_surface_fence.log 2>&1

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CARRY STATE + CARRY-STATE FENCE (added 2026-08-29, capability hunt s0)
# EVIDENCE: desks/mt5/research/carry_state.py -> desks/mt5/data/carry_state.json
#           scripts/check_carry_state.py      -> data/carry_state_report.json
# WHAT WAS MISSING: `grep -i swap desks/mt5/mt5desk/engine.py` returns ZERO hits -- every
# backtest, gate, certificate and forward clock on this desk charges overnight financing at
# exactly 0.00. `mt5desk/financing.py` built the entire verdict API for it and returned
# UNMEASURED forever because "the broker's actual swap table is not in this repo"; it HAS been
# since 2026-08-26 (82 hourly panels x 248 symbols in intelligence/broker_swaps, plus the
# swap_mode units in tape/contract_terms) and nothing read either store. First run (2026-08-29):
# 404 of 496 sides priced, 14 of 17 LIVE sleeves carrying a material uncharged leg -- XAUUSD
# long -57.58/lot/night, which is 48.6% of that sleeve's expectancy and 2.88x the 20.00 rate the
# published null assumed. 132 sides are CARRY-PAID (XAUUSD short +28.12/lot/night, booked at
# zero) -- the false-null direction, which kills real edges with no alert anywhere.
# CADENCE: daily, after the overnight rollover has repriced the panel and after cost_surface, so
# the whole cost basis (spread surface + financing leg) refreshes as one before shadow_forward's
# 07:58 pass. The ORDER is the load-bearing part, not the minute.
# CONFIDENCE: inferred slot. The fence exits 2 on CARRY-UNCHARGED, CARRY-FLIP, STALE,
# STATE-MISSING, UNMEASURED and NO-LIVE-SLEEVES, and never renders an unmeasured side as OK
# (L1.28a). NO-LIVE-SLEEVES is its own status so an empty population cannot report a vacuous
# pass (L1.57), and UNCLASSIFIED (rate known, spread basis absent) is kept distinct from
# UNMEASURED (rate unknown) so a consumer cannot refuse a rate the desk actually holds.
40 6 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python desks/mt5/research/carry_state.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/carry_state.log 2>&1
50 6 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python scripts/check_carry_state.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/carry_state_fence.log 2>&1

# --- ORPHANABLE WRITERS (added 2026-08-29, frontier_unified) -------------------------------
# WHY THIS EXISTS. On 2026-08-28 both FX Blue harvesters reported row 50 while their output
# held 28 rows: `desks/mt5/data/` is git-TRACKED, this box checks it out every ten minutes
# (auto_push) and hourly (the cycle), and a long-running writer that holds an append handle
# open keeps writing into the inode AFTER the name has been unlinked. Nothing errors, nothing
# warns, a reader sees a clean short file, and ~500 harvested records were lost.
# The defect is a SHAPE, not a path -- an append handle held open across a loop that waits on
# network, sleep or a subprocess -- so it recurs in whatever directory is written next. The
# fence looks for the shape, restricted to targets git actually tracks (a gitignored artifact
# has no checkout to eat it), and prints the repair with each hit.
# EVIDENCE: scripts/check_orphanable_writers.py; exit 1 = at least one unrepaired writer.
# A writer that stages outside the tree and publishes in one pass declares ORPHAN-SAFE and
# stops reporting; today that is fxblue_track_record_miner and cohort_and_identity.
41 7 * * * cd "$QUANT_ROOT" && .venv/bin/python scripts/check_orphanable_writers.py >> data/cro_ai_logs/orphanable_writers_fence.log 2>&1

